{"kind":"assert","text":"Declared-acts stages 2 and 3: ownership and acceptance clarification.\n\n1. Stage 2 (fd6f00b6) owns Room admission and the shared policy vocabulary exports. Stage 3 (1e8fee4b) owns all packages/log grammar decoding, roster replay and D(s) semantic verification. Stage-2 condition 1 names five former fixed lists as the overall replacement inventory; its log/decode.ts and log/roster.ts entries are delivered by stage 3, not by a second semantic implementation in stage 2. Before submitting stage 2, remove its two mechanical log import/list edits unless they are already inherited from an independently reviewed stage-3 delivery. Stage 3 uses the frozen contract legacy description and shared policy exports and owns any required log import changes.\n\n2. Parallel development remains allowed. Stage 3 currently consumes policy vocabulary exports introduced by stage 2, so its final standalone review head must include reviewed stage 2. Prefer stage-2 review and landing, then merge that main into stage 3, reconcile every overlapping path, rerun appropriate gates and submit stage 3. A combined candidate is possible only with an explicit request covering both implementation bindings, full artifact inventory and every acceptance condition; a review of one isolated head cannot approve the other. Stage-2 report identifies the log inventory items transferred here; stage-3 report identifies this prerequisite and the complete composition.\n\n3. Stage-3 condition 2 deliberately brings required-call derivation, rebuilt inputs and budget progression, prepared-event checking and the two-version fixture forward from stage 6. All stated stage-3 acceptance remains required. Derivation must account for omitted and extra required calls, including carry eligibility; a recorded context cannot serve as authority for fields the fold can reconstruct. If the early implementation retains land obligations, reviews, notify reviewers or carry eligibility/facts from room-supplied contexts, name those gaps and the required next change; do not describe condition 2 or the full request as satisfied. Unsupported versions are verifier limits, not success. No weakened fixture or partial report closes the full request.\n\n4. Stage 4 still owns production primitives and emission of prepared/reservation-ended, after stage 2. Stage 3 may prove its verifier against valid signed fixtures without waiting for the production emitter. The real Room-to-published-log-to-fresh-clone proof waits for stage 4 and is retained explicitly in stage 6. Stage 6 remains a separate request after stages 3 and 4: complete obligation/evidence/thread fold, required calls and reconstructed contexts, derived effects and first refusal, witness and prepared-event requirements, Git-present comparison and honest Git-unwitnessed limits, streaming/bounds, clock-event ordering, all section-4.7 adversarial fixtures and honest-log controls, and retained steps versions with section-3.9 two-version/deploy-without-activation/exact-retry cases. Earlier proofs are reused with precise coverage, never used to delete an obligation. Any unresolved stage-3 acceptance must remain open in its request; stage 6 is not a reason to waive it.\n\n5. All seven stages and every existing acceptance requirement stay in scope. Stages 4/5 and 6/7 retain their separate ownership, dependencies and review gates. This clarification establishes review and composition boundaries; it approves no source, deploy or live provider call.","body":{"no_git_artifact":"true","stage2":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:fd6f00b612d68c035cbdbc3f27ebe3c21500f079","stage3":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:1e8fee4bfcb6e057bbf352faba2b5719cd39f9c7"}}